Usually for this kind of thing, there's no need to check the closest_id < 0, because any distance will always be smaller than FLT_MAX.

The d < closest_dist and (d == closest_dist) are usually better combined then separated with a later check, i.e.
```
if (d <= closest_dist)
{
    if (d == closest_dist) ....
}
```
