Sure, [`requestPointerCapture()`](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/View#requestPointerCapture()) and [`releasePointerCapture()`](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/View#releasePointerCapture()) were introduced in API level 26. Since we support API level 18 and up, on devices running version < 26, you would get a crash since the methods you're invoking via jni are not available.

To counter that, you can add proxy methods in `Godot.java` as shown below:
```
void requestPointerCapture() {
    if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.O) {
        mRenderView.requestPointerCapture();
    }
    // Do nothing otherwise.
}

// Same for releasePointerCapture()
```

