I see 3 options, and "user allocate, user free" seems to be the cleanest one for me.

## User allocate, user free. It's clear who's responsible for memory managemnt.
```c++
size_t size = 0;
gdnative_string_to_latin1_chars(str, null, &size); // Function return size
char *buffer = (char *)gdnative_alloc(size);
gdnative_string_to_latin1_chars(str, buffer, &size); // Function copy data

//use  it

